OL,3,AKing's role is not policy making, says
OL,4,APalace in slavery apology row
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe King is to deliver a speech on
OL,7,FTuesday which is expected to recognise
OL,8,Fthe painful legacy of slavery. But his
OL,9,Fspeech will reflect the position of the
OL,10,FUK government.
OL,12,FUK Prime Minister Andy Burnham had
OL,13,Fsuggested there could be some form of
OL,14,Fapology over slavery, but has ruled out
OL,15,Ffinancial reparations.
